<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chichimeca</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chichimecs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chichimeca was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahuatl">Nahuatl</a> name for the nomadic and semi-nomadic peoples of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, and also for migrants from the north who settled in central Mexico. Several <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahuas">Nahua</a> city-states, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texcoco">Texcoco</a>, claimed Chichimec ancestry. In the 16th century the Chichimeca resisted Spanish expansion in the long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chichimeca-war">Chichimeca War</a> of about 1550-1590.</p></div>
